From 15c9e4247e8d7599d03784dd52b5aac3233e6f16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sukrit Jaidee <45908411+SukritJaAIproject@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:16:16 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/18] feat(desktop): detection policies and training-station
 rows (1.3.0 groundwork)

Detection policy (for the ISO 15118 edition):
- desktop/runtime/detection_policy.py: whitelisted policies ("baseline",
  "iso15118-standard" = ISO 15118-2 rule layer + ISO 15118-3 SLAC timers,
  normative). apply_env() clears inherited research switches (EV_AI_NPD_RULE,
  EV_AI_SLAC_WAIT, ...) and sets the policy's before any detector module is
  imported; verify_loaded() raises if the imported modules disagree
  (ISO_IN_VECTOR must stay off: the packaged weights are 33 features wide).
- The policy comes from summary.json detectionPolicy (absent = baseline), so
  the detector runs under the policy its bundled benchmark was measured with.
  serve() passes it with Agentic AI's real leaderboard rank to every worker
  (replacing the hard-coded benchmarkRank 1); /health and the PCAP result
  report it; an unknown id marks the sidecar not ready instead of guessing.
- Vendored core/iso15118.py and core/iso_features.py (needed once EV_AI_ISO=1)
  and listed them in the PyInstaller spec; stop attribution knows the
  [V2G2-711] / [V2G2-443] / [V2G2-448] rule alerts.
- export_summary.py copies detectionPolicy from results/run_manifest.json.

Training-station rows (212-station view):
- load_fault_detection_summary(train_records=...) adds analysis.byStationTrain
  from an in-sample replay (64 MiB cap), rows tagged split="train"; held-out
  rows are tagged split="test". Checks: no overlap with held-out stations,
  station set == split.json train, totals equal the replay's leaderboard.
  The held-out gates, totals, leaderboard and snapshot date are unchanged.
- export_summary.py --train-records (or IMPS_FAULT_TRAIN_RECORDS).
- api.ts/data.ts: optional split, byStationTrain and detectionPolicy; an
  unknown split value is rejected, held-out rows must add up to the dataset;
  helpers allStationRows / heldOutStationTotals / stationSplitOf; tests.
- Hero shows a "Standard rules" chip and the PCAP result names the policy
  when it is not the baseline.

